  "result": "Perfect! All 125 tests pass. I've successfully created the dates module:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n\u2705 **src/dates.js** \u2014 New module for UTC date handling:\n- `isValidDate(text)`: Validates 'YYYY-MM-DD' format and checks date validity (handles leap years, month boundaries, etc.)\n- `addDays(date, n)`: Adds/subtracts n days to a date, working in UTC\n- `daysBetween(a, b)`: Calculates whole days between two dates (b - a) in UTC\n\n\u2705 **src/invoices.js** \u2014 Updated to use dates module:\n- Imported `isValidDate` from `src/dates.js`\n- Removed local `isValidDate` function\n- createInvoice now uses the centralized date validation\n\n\u2705 **test/dates.test.js** \u2014 Comprehensive test suite (16 tests):\n- Valid date acceptance (including leap year edge cases)\n- Invalid format and date rejection\n- Adding days (positive, negative, month/year boundaries, leap years)\n- Calculating days between dates (positive, negative, leap years)\n- Error handling for invalid dates\n- UTC consistency verification\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- All dates are `'YYYY-MM-DD'` strings (consistent format)\n- All date arithmetic is done in UTC using `T00:00:00Z` to avoid timezone issues\n- `daysBetween` uses floor division to get whole days only\n- Functions throw descriptive errors on invalid input\n- Properly handles leap years (2000, 2024 yes; 1900, 2025 no)\n- Centralized date validation used throughout the system",
